' Declarations for Roku runtime interfaces BrighterScript does not ship with.
'
' A .d.bs file is never transpiled, so nothing here reaches the device - it only
' documents and type-checks members BrighterScript would otherwise flag.
'
' Note that declaring a class does NOT satisfy the CreateObject() component
' check (BS1129): that check consults BrighterScript's own bundled component
' list, which contains no screen components beyond roScreen and roSGScreen, and
' it cannot be extended. The roKeyboardScreen call in main.bs is therefore
' suppressed at the call site as well. This file stays because it records the
' members the call site relies on, and because a future BrighterScript may well
' resolve CreateObject() from declarations and make the suppression redundant.

' Modal text entry. Only the main thread may run it: Show() blocks on a Wait,
' which a component script must not do.
class roKeyboardScreen
    public title as string
    public text as string
    public buttons as object
    sub setMessagePort(port as object)
    end sub
    sub Show()
    end sub
end class
